WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.920
<i>In Toronto's war on crime.</i>

2
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.400
<i>the worst offenders
are pursued by the detectives</i>

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.920
<i>of the Specialized Criminal
Investigations Unit.</i>

4
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.230
<i>These are their stories.</i>

5
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.400
Alright. I'm just gonna
need your signature.

6
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.260
Here and here.

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.050
And that should do it.

8
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.020
This isn't
a big mistake. right?

9
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.400
I'm gonna let you in on
a little secret. Melissa.

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.780
There are no mistakes
in Toronto real estate.

11
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.090
He's not wrong.

12
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.430
Nothing can be bought
that can't be sold again.

13
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.950
At a markup.
- Right.

14
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.810
And if I just want a good home?

15
00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.600
Listen. it's nerve-wracking.
I get it.

16
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.980
All this gobbledegook.

17
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.950
But it's a great little home.

18
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.290
You're gonna be
very happy there.

19
00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.120
Mr. Henning.

20
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.710
tell her. how often do
we get home buyers

21
00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.400
having last-minute jitters?

22
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.020
- First time?
- Mm-hmm.

23
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.980
Well. then I would be worried
if you weren't nervous.

24
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:10.540
And that covers it.
How do you feel. Paul?

25
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.540
I mean. yeah. Good.

26
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.470
Lot of good memories here.
But a new chapter awaits.

27
00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.160
Japan. That's exciting.

28
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.810
When are you thinking
about going back?

29
00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.400
Soon as this is finalized.

30
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.950
It won't be much
longer now. right?

31
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.880
No inspections. no conditions.

32
00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.850
The funds should be
released tomorrow.

33
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:29.990
Oh. excuse me.

34
00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.990
Samantha Morgan.

35
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.260
Yeah?

36
00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.670
Wow. wow. wow. wow.
Wait. wait.

37
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.570
How is that even possible?

38
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.710
You checked yourself?

39
00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.090
Yeah. Leave him to me.

40
00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:58.330
Oh. hey.

41
00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.670
I'm sorry to bother you. but you
wouldn't happen to have a. uh.

42
00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:02.710
flashlight on your
cellphone. would you?

43
00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:04.190
I dropped my keys...

44
00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.500
I-I mean
I'm sure they-they're

45
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.330
in the brush here somewhere.
- Oh. yeah. sure.

46
00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.290
You wouldn't mind?
Thanks a lot.

47
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.470
Hey. I'll say. Paul?

48
00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.980
- Have we met?
- Paul Phillips.

49
00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.090
The same Paul Phillips
that lives over on Alton Drive.

50
00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:20.120
Yeah. but I... I'm sorry.
but how do you know my name?

51
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.780
I'm drawing a blank.
- I bet you are.

52
00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.980
What the hell is...

53
00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.600
Oh. my God. Guys? Guys!

54
00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:36.190
So... who do we have here?

55
00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:37.850
White male. 40s.

56
00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.290
Doesn't look like he was
using the skate park.

57
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.920
Wounds look like
a double-edged blade.

58
00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.430
Two. three. four quick jabs.

59
00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.230
The one in the groin
would have finished him off.

60
00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:53.290
And the blood trail suggests
he was stabbed on the path.

61
00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.570
dragged here

62
00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.020
as he was dying.

63
00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.500
I don't see any
defensive wounds.

64
00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.740
It wasn't much of a fight.
- Happened fast.

65
00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.670
Maybe he was facing his attacker

66
00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.290
but didn't expect violence.

67
00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.710
You think he knew him?

68
00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.740
A stranger approaches
on a dark path.

69
00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.430
you put your guard up.

70
00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.160
Friend approaches.
you don't end up dead.

71
00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.710
Fair call.

72
00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:18.230
Hmm. no visible tattoos.
no discolouration of the skin

73
00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.920
to indicate missing watch
or jewellery.

74
00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.290
Nondescript clothes.

75
00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.670
neutral-coloured shoes
off the rack.

76
00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.020
Blank slate.

77
00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.920
His fingerprints aren't
in the system

78
00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.360
and there's no match
for missing persons.

79
00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.780
Doesn't come home last night.

80
00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.120
doesn't show up for work
this morning.

81
00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.290
nobody's missing this guy.

82
00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.260
Apparently not.

83
00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.810
Empty pockets. no car keys.
no phone. no wallet. nothing.

84
00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.500
Simple mugging?
Cleaned him out?

85
00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.880
Well. with a mugging you take
the wallet and run.

86
00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.360
You don't drag the guy
into the woods.

87
00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.470
Well. I'd say
you don't have much to go on.

88
00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:49.980
but this is nothing to go on.

89
00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:51.710
Report on your John Doe.

90
00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.360
Nothing much to write
home about.

91
00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.300
- Well. that's on brand.
- But there is this.

92
00:05:58.540 --> 00:05:59.950
Black molars.

93
00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.850
That's silver diamine fluoride.

94
00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:04.190
Correct. Topical treatment
for tooth decay.

95
00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.430
an alternative to drilling.

96
00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.540
Stains the teeth.
- Thank you.

97
00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:10.400
So. our John Doe didn't
wanna get cavities.

98
00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.740
That's not exactly a lead.

99
00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.400
I hate to break it to you.

100
00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.120
but I see some canvassing
in your future.

101
00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.090
Get a digital rendering made
and go talk to the public.

102
00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.300
The public.

103
00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.290
Take a close look.

104
00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.230
Yeah.
Yeah. he came in last night.

105
00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.740
Alright. so you've
seen him before?

106
00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.920
No. but he tipped big.

107
00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:38.160
Stuck around to eat and said
he just cashed in his chips?

108
00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:40.980
There.

109
00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:42.950
May I? Thank you.

110
00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.810
Okay. 9:42 PM.

111
00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:52.600
No calls. no texts.
He's just dining alone.

112
00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:54.920
I don't know.
Fried chicken and sudoku?

113
00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.570
Looks pretty good to me.

114
00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.160
Hey. look at that.

115
00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.920
The pen.

116
00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.980
Right there.

117
00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:05.600
He just throws it in the trash
with everything else. but...

118
00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:12.090
He came in with it. See?

119
00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:13.810
Maybe there's a logo on it.

120
00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.400
It's a reach.
but it's something.

121
00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.600
This path leads us to
a dumpster full of old chicken.

122
00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:19.260
doesn't it?

123
00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.600
You're in luck. It was late.
I already emptied the trash.

124
00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:23.360
so anything he tossed
is still in the can.

125
00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:26.470
Could we borrow a pizza box?

126
00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:32.260
Talking to the public?
Garbage search?

127
00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.020
This guy is starting
to bother me.

128
00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.710
Oh. come on.
You love it.

129
00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:41.880
Oh. God.

130
00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.290
Hey.

131
00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.430
There we go.

132
00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:51.500
Samantha Morgan.
Wingrove Realty.

133
00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:53.430
Well. it's not nothing...

134
00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.500
I mean. it's Paul.
Why? What's happened?

135
00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.920
- And how do you know him?
- I sold his house for him.

136
00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.980
I'm actually here
grabbing my staging materials.

137
00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:06.740
He cashed in his chips.

138
00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:08.470
Excuse me?

139
00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:10.430
Is he okay?

140
00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:12.190
I am afraid he was
found dead this morning.

141
00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:14.670
What? What on earth happened?

142
00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:17.050
Uh. we don't actually have
a lot of details right now.

143
00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.640
But maybe you can help.
This image is a rendering.

144
00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.500
Do you happen to have anything
that could help us confirm

145
00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.470
that we're talking
about the same person?

146
00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.230
I mean... that's him.

147
00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.500
I'm 100% sure that's him.
Hold on.

148
00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:37.810
Yeah. that's our guy.

149
00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:39.570
Do you mind
if I hang on to this?

150
00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.990
- No. of course.
- Thanks.

151
00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:48.290
I... I'm sorry. I'm just
a little confused here.

152
00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.640
He was on his way back to Japan.

153
00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.540
- Japan?
- Yeah. that's where he worked.

154
00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:54.230
That's why he wanted
to get rid of this place.

155
00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:55.710
He was spending most
of his time there.

156
00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:58.190
Yeah. well. that explains
why no one misses him.

157
00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:00.880
Are there any photos
of his friends or family?

158
00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.740
Any personal items?

159
00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:04.880
Usually we haul that stuff
out by the truckload.

160
00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.500
But we actually had to bring
some tchotchkes in.

161
00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.850
Yeah. there's
not much character.

162
00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:13.050
Did you happen to meet
anyone else in his life?

163
00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.850
No. We only met
a couple weeks ago.

164
00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:16.570
That deal must've gone
through pretty quick.

165
00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:19.020
We priced it to move. He was
eager to go back overseas.

166
00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.850
Hm. Thanks.

167
00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:23.400
Listen. uh...

168
00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:26.050
Everyone's signing the line
here. so just curious.

169
00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:28.360
Will this affect the sale?

170
00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.810
I... I don't mean to be crass.

171
00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:31.920
It's. uh. not my department.

172
00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.570
Yeah. it's Detective Bateman.

173
00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.710
I was hoping you could
run a name for me.

174
00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:40.020
Yeah. Paul Philips.
Date of birth. March 23rd. 1981.

175
00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:42.540
Address. 227 Alton Drive.

176
00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:46.360
Search CPIC. check occurrences.
see what you can find on. uh.

177
00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:47.950
next of kin. emergency contacts.

178
00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:49.600
Thanks.

179
00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.740
None of the neighbours have
seen this guy for months.

180
00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.470
Anything out of
the ordinary lately?

181
00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:55.430
Oh. just some real estate
people coming and going.

182
00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:58.780
One of the neighbours.
he was so irritated.

183
00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:03.260
Place sold for 1.5 under market.
Devalues the block. poor thing.

184
00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.050
Yeah?

185
00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.990
Okay. Thank you so much.

186
00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:11.880
Paul Philips has a sister
in Scarborough.

187
00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.920
- There you go.
- Thank you.

188
00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.640
I just can't make sense of it.

189
00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:17.050
- We're so sorry for your loss.
- Who would do that to Paul?

190
00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:19.290
Well. that's something
we're hoping you might be able

191
00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:21.020
to help us figure out.

192
00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.570
Uh. but first. Lydia.

193
00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.670
because of the circumstances
of your brother's death.

194
00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:27.980
we do need to confirm
his identity.

195
00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.090
Is that something
you're comfortable doing?

196
00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:31.470
Oh...

197
00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.640
Oh. God.

198
00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.430
Yeah.

199
00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.120
Okay.

200
00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.360
Chellas. second opinion.

201
00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.780
What are the bruises
around the. uh. stab wounds?

202
00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:46.980
Well. they're from the attack.

203
00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:49.600
Looks like the murder
weapon had a hilt.

204
00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.640
Why? Something bothering
you. Detective?

205
00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:53.570
Only everything.

206
00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.710
It's all set up in there.

207
00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:05.640
You can take your time and we'll
go in when you're ready.

208
00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.640
- Okay.
- Miss Philips.

209
00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.230
Uh. were you aware your brother
was back in town?

210
00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:11.190
No. um. it was weird.

211
00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:13.230
He usually let me know
when he was coming.

212
00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:15.740
At any rate.
Detective Graff and I.

213
00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:17.780
we will give you
a moment to yourself

214
00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.540
because we understand
this is difficult.

215
00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.160
Did you know
he'd sold his house?

216
00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:22.570
He did?

217
00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:24.850
Yeah. he was in a rush
to get rid of it.

218
00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:27.470
Took far less than he could've.
How often were you two in touch?

219
00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.810
Well. not daily.

220
00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.670
but you know. we shared
the big stuff.

221
00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:34.850
- Like selling his home.
- I would've thought so. Yeah.

222
00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.400
I think I'm ready
to see him now.

223
00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.190
Alright. Right this way.

224
00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.880
That was something
else we shared.

225
00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.920
We were both
blind as bats.

226
00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:45.160
Only. Paul was brave enough
to have the surgery.

227
00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.570
He had laser surgery?

228
00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.920
Yeah. The same astigmatism.
but Paul had his corrected.

229
00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.160
Do you have a number
for Paul in Japan?

230
00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.260
Yes... but aren't
we going in now?

231
00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:58.880
Can you dial it. please?

232
00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.810
Okay...

233
00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:02.810
I'm so sorry.
I'll be right back.

234
00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.230
Hey. what are you thinking?

235
00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:09.740
The stained molars.
The silver diamine fluoride.

236
00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:13.920
Dentists use it when a patient
has an aversion to anesthetic.

237
00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:18.470
If he can't have anesthetic.
he didn't get eye surgery.

238
00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:21.090
Well. maybe he's not
a blank slate after all.

239
00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:23.430
- Paul?
<i>- Lydia?</i>

240
00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:27.020
- You're alive!
- Lydia? Is everything okay?

241
00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:29.400
So who's in the morgue?

242
00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:31.230
An imposter.

243
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.120
I don't understand.

244
00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:44.290
If that wasn't Paul Philips.
who was he?

245
00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.190
Let's start with
a different question.

246
00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:48.710
How does one sell a house
they don't own?

247
00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:51.360
He had ID. I showed you.

248
00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:53.090
Two pieces.
that's the requirement.

249
00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:54.780
Which you didn't authenticate.

250
00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:57.330
I checked his photo.
I looked at his face.

251
00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.670
I mean. I'm not Interpol.

252
00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:03.090
You met him two weeks ago.
he came to you. Is that right?

253
00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:04.880
He saw my bus stop ad.

254
00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.360
Told me he was in a hurry

255
00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.230
and that I should take
any reasonable offer.

256
00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.120
Nothing about that
seemed suspicious?

257
00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:12.540
That's a motivated seller.
That's music to my ears.

258
00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:14.260
Keep everything moving so fast

259
00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.920
that nobody notices
anything's off?

260
00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.710
Like clearing a house
of all personal items.

261
00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.470
Not a single photo or keepsake

262
00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:22.740
that might identify
the real Paul Philips.

263
00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.120
His name was on the title.

264
00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:26.090
Oh. funny you should say.

265
00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.330
He spelled his name wrong
on the. uh. purchase agreement.

266
00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:31.670
Used the. uh. common
spelling of Phillips.

267
00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:34.020
Two L's rather than

268
00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.430
the one L that the real
Paul Philips used.

269
00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.020
Repeats the error a few times.

270
00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.780
Uh. obviously...
I didn't see that.

271
00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:42.500
Samantha. have you
heard of anything like this

272
00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.230
happening before?

273
00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:47.120
I mean. I've heard of it.
but no. not to anyone I know.

274
00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.400
Hey. who do you like in.
uh. financial crimes?

275
00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.290
Like? Strong word.

276
00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.740
Chase is alright.

277
00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.430
Thank you.

278
00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:01.950
Title theft.
Yeah. it's a booming business.

279
00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.640
That's what you get
when a starter home

280
00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:05.290
costs a million bucks.

281
00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.090
Safeguards haven't
kept up to the money

282
00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:08.920
and the bad guys
have taken note.

283
00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.780
Have a seat.

284
00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:16.500
In this case. the. uh.
fraudster poses the homeowner.

285
00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:17.810
Fake. uh--
- Fake ID?

286
00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.290
Owner overseas?

287
00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:21.050
Right. Obviously.

288
00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:22.780
They target vacant properties.

289
00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:25.190
Unmowed lawns.
junk mail piling up.

290
00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.430
They do a title search.
find out the owner's name.

291
00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:29.430
Little bit of
rudimentary identity theft

292
00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:31.190
and they are
well on their way.

293
00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.780
Here.
- What's this?

294
00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.740
30 homes in the GTA
in the last three years.

295
00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.740
sold or mortgaged without
the owner's consent.

296
00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.160
Oh. Jesus.

297
00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:41.850
Was this guy involved
with any of them?

298
00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:43.500
Uh...

299
00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.430
I don't think so.

300
00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:48.300
But that face rings a bell.

301
00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:52.810
Um...

302
00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:55.120
Move.

303
00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:57.880
Uh. there was a similar
scheme in Vancouver.

304
00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:01.120
There was a guy who rent an
apartment to 19 people at once.

305
00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.810
Collected rent from all of them

306
00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.360
and then left before
anyone got wise.

307
00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.470
Is that him?

308
00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:08.920
- Yeah. that's the guy.
- Yeah. that's him.

309
00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.740
Vancouver Regional Police
never caught him.

310
00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.810
but they appealed to the public
and they did get a name.

311
00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:16.050
Timothy Fox was posing
as Paul Philips. huh?

312
00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.920
Who are you working
with in financial?

313
00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:22.160
Oh. well. Graff is a big fan
of Chase. so we're using her.

314
00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:24.740
Yeah. one more day and Fox
would've got away with it.

315
00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:26.500
but luckily the house
is still in escrow.

316
00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.600
so the sale never went through.
- Well. that's your angle.

317
00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.710
Somebody solved that problem
with a knife.

318
00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.810
Yeah. most of the funds
at risk were the bank's.

319
00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:35.190
All insured.
However. the buyer's deposit...

320
00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:36.980
Gotta be over a hundred grand.

321
00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:38.850
That's killing money.

322
00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.330
Go meet the buyer.

323
00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.160
I've been looking for months.

324
00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:47.160
Got outbid so many times.

325
00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:51.260
Finally. an offer gets accepted
and then this happens.

326
00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.850
It's bad luck.

327
00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:54.190
Yeah. is it true?

328
00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:56.880
That this imposter guy
was murdered?

329
00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:58.470
That's what my real estate
agent told me.

330
00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:01.050
Um. Melissa. how much money
did you put down on the house.

331
00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:02.980
$150.000.

332
00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:04.740
That's a big number.

333
00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:07.430
Yeah. with a big loan
on top of that I bet.

334
00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:10.190
Um. can I ask where you work?

335
00:17:10.190 --> 00:17:12.850
Harbour View Lounge
on Wellington.

336
00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.740
I'm a bartender.
- Oh. yeah?

337
00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:17.780
What's your favourite cocktail?
Not to mix. but to drink.

338
00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:20.330
I. myself. am fond
of a Gin Rickey.

339
00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.330
Well. I'm not drinking
much these days.

340
00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:25.400
- Oh. because you're pregnant?
- Excuse me?

341
00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:28.120
That's why you want more
living space. Baby on the way.

342
00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:30.430
And how rude do you have
to be to make that leap?

343
00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:33.470
Well. the leap happened
earlier. From this.

344
00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:35.330
Plaster of Paris.

345
00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:38.780
Clay powder.

346
00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.740
Mounting plaque.

347
00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.230
I don't see any other
crafting supplies about.

348
00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:47.290
So. uh. I'm assuming it's a
moulding kit for your baby foot.

349
00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:48.640
That was the leap.

350
00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:51.780
The no drinking part just.

351
00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:54.330
uh. confirmed it.

352
00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:57.190
Or did I get it wrong?

353
00:17:57.190 --> 00:17:59.610
I'm four months pregnant.

354
00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:03.330
Did your parents
co-sign for the house?

355
00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:05.740
No. And that's none
of your business.

356
00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:07.540
And what about
the father to be?

357
00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.980
Not in the picture and even
less of your business.

358
00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:12.500
- Where were you two nights ago?
- Is he serious?

359
00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:15.330
Well. the man who tried
to steal $150.000 from you

360
00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:17.950
was killed.
so he's quite serious.

361
00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.190
I was at work.

362
00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:23.640
Mondays are slow. so maybe
only 300 people saw me?

363
00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.120
Would you like their names?

364
00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.330
Let's start with
your manager's phone number.

365
00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:34.190
You went. uh.
pretty hard at her.

366
00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:36.600
I'm not getting stabby vibes.
Are you?

367
00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:38.740
No. but she's definitely
hiding something.

368
00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:42.160
She didn't even ask if she was
getting her deposit back.

369
00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.850
That money's dodgy.
Let's follow it.

370
00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:52.190
Yes. I was the advisor on
Miss Auerbach's file.

371
00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:53.430
Meaning you approved
the loan?

372
00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.360
- I processed it.
- Is there a difference?

373
00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.470
Detectives.
I'm sure you understand

374
00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.230
you've got us in a spot here.

375
00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:01.670
We can't discuss the personal
finances of a client

376
00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.050
without a court order.

377
00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:05.400
The finances
of a single bartender

378
00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:07.430
who buys a house for $1.500.000?

379
00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.710
I know it can seem opaque
from the outside.

380
00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.670
but the industry uses something
called a GDS ratio--

381
00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.430
Gross Debt Services.

382
00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:15.540
The percentage of income
that goes toward housing.

383
00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:17.540
- You know your stuff.
- I do.

384
00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:19.710
Yeah. I learned the hard way
when I tried to buy in Roncy

385
00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:21.260
on a cop salary.

386
00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:23.430
But. uh. by my math.

387
00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.330
to get approved for that loan.

388
00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:28.920
Melissa Auerbach would have to
be making over $200.000 a year?

389
00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:32.740
Yeah. she's a charming lady.
but. uh. that's a lot of tips.

390
00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:35.050
She had all the records
to back it up.

391
00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:37.470
- Bank statements? Tax returns?
- Yup. All of it.

392
00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.090
And you authenticated these?

393
00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:41.430
We asked for official
documents and she supplied them.

394
00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:44.160
Detectives. as the bank's
manager. I have to insist.

395
00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.360
Get a court order and you can
look at the records yourself.

396
00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:49.330
If you insist.

397
00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:57.260
Someone definitely
cooked the books.

398
00:19:57.260 --> 00:20:00.090
Made the. uh. finances
look peachy in one blink.

399
00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.470
Hmm.
- What is it?

400
00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:05.090
Maybe that was
Timothy Fox's mistake.

401
00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:08.360
His con ran into
an even bigger con.

402
00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:12.090
An imposter meets a forger in
a dark alley and blood spills?

403
00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:14.740
Maybe it's time we run
a con of our own.

404
00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:17.470
You still interested
in buying a house?

405
00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:21.980
- Have you been looking long?
- I just started.

406
00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.330
Do I look like a deer
in the headlights?

407
00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:27.950
You'll get the hang of it.
You just need some good help.

408
00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:31.570
About that. I actually
don't have an agent yet

409
00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:33.570
and my friend Melissa
recommended you.

410
00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:35.190
Well. then.

411
00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:38.360
I'm always charming. but now
I'll really pour it on.

412
00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:42.470
Is this the kind of place
you're looking for?

413
00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.430
Oh. I mean
it's beautiful.

414
00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:47.710
But. uh. I don't know.

415
00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.920
See. here's the thing.

416
00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:52.880
Our finances are a bit tricky.

417
00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:55.850
I'm a gallery owner. my
husband. Henry is a carpenter.

418
00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:59.880
We're doing fine. but a lot
of our income is in cash.

419
00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:03.780
meaning it doesn't necessarily
all make its way to the books.

420
00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:06.470
That's between you and God.

421
00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.670
Okay. it's just on paper

422
00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:10.400
we don't qualify for
much of a mortgage.

423
00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:13.850
None of my business.
but what you're describing.

424
00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:15.600
I see it all the time.

425
00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:19.430
In fact. I know someone who
helps clients in your situation.

426
00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:22.600
- Like a mortgage broker?
- Uh. more like an advisor.

427
00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:25.020
He'll help you organize
your books.

428
00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:28.190
Oh. I mean. we don't wanna
do anything unethical.

429
00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:30.950
Oh. of course not.
You just want a home.

430
00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:32.950
You'll make
your payments. right?

431
00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:35.810
- Yeah. of course.
- Then no one gets hurt.

432
00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:40.330
Jesse Grayson.

433
00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.190
Let him do his thing.

434
00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.470
you'll have the home of your
dreams before you know it.

435
00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:48.740
So what would you do?

436
00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:50.640
My idea for a restaurant

437
00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:52.230
is vegan on one side.

438
00:21:52.230 --> 00:21:54.230
snout to tail meat on the other.

439
00:21:54.230 --> 00:21:55.950
Okay. perfect.
Offend everyone.

440
00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:58.330
Appeal to everyone!
That's the move. Dad.

441
00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:00.670
Respect their boundaries.
but all together.

442
00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:03.360
And the servers would use. like.
a demilitarized zone down the--

443
00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:05.330
Oh.

444
00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:10.500
- Who is it?
- Uh. just a colleague.

445
00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:13.120
Why don't you head in?
I'll be right there.

446
00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:14.710
Okay.

447
00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:19.600
What are you
doing here Grayson?

448
00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:22.230
- What'd you say to the cops?
- You're following me?

449
00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:24.260
I had to make sure you
weren't getting cold feet.

450
00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:25.540
Cold feet?

451
00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:27.500
I did not tell you
to kill that guy.

452
00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:29.400
I told you to take care of it--
- Look.

453
00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:30.920
I just came here
so you understand

454
00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:33.120
the reality behind all this.

455
00:22:33.120 --> 00:22:34.810
It's you and me now.

456
00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:38.120
Us. Adrian.

457
00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:39.810
Do you understand?

458
00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:42.880
I didn't say anything
and I won't.

459
00:22:44.190 --> 00:22:46.470
Just stay away from my family.

460
00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:49.670
Later. buddy.

461
00:22:54.330 --> 00:22:57.470
This Grayson guy's got
this pretty nice operation

462
00:22:57.470 --> 00:23:01.260
doctoring people's finances
until Timothy Fox comes along

463
00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:02.640
with his own scheme

464
00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:04.400
and threatens to blow
the whole thing up.

465
00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:05.950
Is that your theory?

466
00:23:05.950 --> 00:23:07.570
Yeah. if Fox had managed
to sell that house.

467
00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:09.050
it would've sparked
a huge investigation

468
00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:10.470
once the real owner
got home from Japan.

469
00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:12.670
And that would've exposed
the whole operation?

470
00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:14.330
Yeah. we're thinking
Grayson killed Fox

471
00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:15.810
before that could happen.

472
00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:18.120
Nullified the sale thinking
that's the end of that.

473
00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:19.400
problem solved.

474
00:23:19.400 --> 00:23:20.850
That's him. We got him.

475
00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:22.990
Location data
from Grayson's phone.

476
00:23:24.430 --> 00:23:27.990
He was at Weston Skatepark
at the time of the killing.

477
00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:40.990
Jesse Grayson! Armed officers!
We're coming in!

478
00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:55.470
Bring them in.

479
00:24:07.570 --> 00:24:10.190
Alas. poor Grayson.

480
00:24:18.090 --> 00:24:19.780
Uh. single blow to the head.

481
00:24:19.780 --> 00:24:22.780
That's most likely
what brought him down.

482
00:24:22.780 --> 00:24:27.740
Follow by repeated blows...

483
00:24:29.260 --> 00:24:31.290
to finish him off.

484
00:24:31.300 --> 00:24:33.190
Left no doubt.

485
00:24:34.950 --> 00:24:37.090
Killer drops his weapon. then...

486
00:24:38.400 --> 00:24:41.950
washes up with alcohol
and high tails it out of here.

487
00:24:41.950 --> 00:24:44.300
Not before taking
the computer.

488
00:24:52.570 --> 00:24:54.360
Forged T4.

489
00:24:54.360 --> 00:24:57.260
Artificially aged.
Coffee ring and all.

490
00:24:57.260 --> 00:25:00.710
This must be where
Grayson did his work.

491
00:25:00.710 --> 00:25:03.470
It's a good bet that all the
clients were on that hard drive.

492
00:25:03.470 --> 00:25:05.500
One of them didn't
want it found.

493
00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:07.260
This crime scene's a mess.

494
00:25:07.260 --> 00:25:09.710
The baton was a weapon
of opportunity.

495
00:25:09.710 --> 00:25:11.290
Came from here.

496
00:25:11.300 --> 00:25:13.540
Grayson was prepared.

497
00:25:13.540 --> 00:25:16.540
Yeah. for a lifetime
of not dating.

498
00:25:16.540 --> 00:25:18.950
That's interesting.

499
00:25:18.950 --> 00:25:24.050
Double-sided blade. quick jabs.
bruising from the guard.

500
00:25:24.050 --> 00:25:26.360
That's the weapon
that killed Timothy Fox?

501
00:25:26.360 --> 00:25:27.470
Could be.

502
00:25:27.470 --> 00:25:29.500
So if Grayson killed Fox.

503
00:25:29.500 --> 00:25:31.540
who killed Grayson?

504
00:25:32.670 --> 00:25:35.710
Someone didn't want Grayson's
handiwork to come to light.

505
00:25:35.710 --> 00:25:37.160
That's why they took
his computer.

506
00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:39.290
Yeah. someone
with enough skin in the game

507
00:25:39.300 --> 00:25:41.020
to go all the way to murder.

508
00:25:41.020 --> 00:25:42.670
Well. that tracks.

509
00:25:42.670 --> 00:25:44.950
Grayson's services would appeal
to all kinds of bad actors.

510
00:25:44.950 --> 00:25:46.540
If you can get a mortgage.
you can launder $1.000.000

511
00:25:46.540 --> 00:25:48.360
in the time
it takes to flip a condo.

512
00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:49.880
Do you have his phone?

513
00:25:49.880 --> 00:25:51.850
I have his call history
from his provider.

514
00:25:51.850 --> 00:25:54.230
- Nothing?
- Well. couple of maybes.

515
00:25:54.230 --> 00:25:57.230
Uh. some numbered of companies.
some. uh. foreign owners.

516
00:25:57.230 --> 00:25:58.810
a couple of pay-as-you-go's.

517
00:25:58.810 --> 00:26:00.330
but nothing that
connects to real estate.

518
00:26:00.330 --> 00:26:01.780
Or criminal associates.

519
00:26:01.780 --> 00:26:04.400
Um. we thought somebody
of your expertise

520
00:26:04.400 --> 00:26:06.880
might be able to spot
something we'd missed.

521
00:26:06.880 --> 00:26:08.540
How many listings
are we talking about?

522
00:26:12.400 --> 00:26:14.120
Alright. let me sit with it.

523
00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:16.330
- Well. I think we--
- Alone.

524
00:26:25.230 --> 00:26:27.920
Hey. Bob. How's the tree house
coming along?

525
00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:30.470
The kids want second floor
and plumbing.

526
00:26:30.470 --> 00:26:32.500
Let me know if you need help
with financing.

527
00:26:34.050 --> 00:26:36.330
Yeah. have a good night.
Adrian.

528
00:26:55.850 --> 00:26:59.260
Sorry. Sorry. Tamara.
I had to work late.

529
00:27:04.330 --> 00:27:07.050
And I should've called.

530
00:27:07.050 --> 00:27:08.740
Would've been nice.

531
00:27:15.230 --> 00:27:17.260
Hey.

532
00:27:18.640 --> 00:27:20.260
I'm sorry.

533
00:27:38.190 --> 00:27:40.500
You think she's okay in there?

534
00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:42.470
Well. I offered her food.

535
00:27:42.470 --> 00:27:45.120
She made a sound I...
didn't recognize.

536
00:27:45.120 --> 00:27:47.570
Bateman! Graff!

537
00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:52.470
We were on the wrong path.
- What do you mean?

538
00:27:52.470 --> 00:27:54.120
It's not one
of Grayson's clients.

539
00:27:54.120 --> 00:27:55.920
He starts the loans. yes.

540
00:27:55.920 --> 00:27:57.980
But someone still needs
to underrate them.

541
00:27:57.990 --> 00:28:00.160
I looked at
the land title registry

542
00:28:00.160 --> 00:28:01.500
and that's when I saw it.

543
00:28:01.500 --> 00:28:02.920
The lending institutions.

544
00:28:02.920 --> 00:28:05.360
The same ones keep coming up
over and over again

545
00:28:05.360 --> 00:28:07.740
and that's what Grayson's
computer would have shown you.

546
00:28:07.740 --> 00:28:11.400
They're all getting
their dodgy financing

547
00:28:11.400 --> 00:28:13.850
from Hemisphere Savings & Loans.

548
00:28:13.850 --> 00:28:17.360
So our big fish
isn't a gangster.

549
00:28:17.360 --> 00:28:19.360
He's a banker.

550
00:28:23.020 --> 00:28:25.050
Hot diggity damn.

551
00:28:27.190 --> 00:28:29.230
That's a beautiful view.

552
00:28:29.230 --> 00:28:30.810
Beautiful home.

553
00:28:30.810 --> 00:28:32.570
Yeah. what can I do for you?

554
00:28:32.570 --> 00:28:35.160
Uh. tell me. uh. Mr. Henning.

555
00:28:35.160 --> 00:28:37.160
A man in your position.

556
00:28:37.160 --> 00:28:40.920
is your compensation tied to
the performance of your branch?

557
00:28:42.190 --> 00:28:44.190
There is an incentive
structure. yes.

558
00:28:44.190 --> 00:28:47.020
So. if a branch does well.
you do well.

559
00:28:47.020 --> 00:28:49.850
That's obvious that. uh.
it's doing very well.

560
00:28:49.850 --> 00:28:51.640
I have a good team.

561
00:28:51.640 --> 00:28:54.090
Transferred there three years
ago. we gelled right away.

562
00:28:54.090 --> 00:28:56.740
Uh. Mr. Henning. we're here
because we found evidence

563
00:28:56.740 --> 00:28:59.260
of widespread fraud
at your branch.

564
00:28:59.260 --> 00:29:01.670
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

565
00:29:01.670 --> 00:29:03.470
And we also have
reason to believe

566
00:29:03.470 --> 00:29:05.470
that these crimes
are connected to two murders.

567
00:29:05.470 --> 00:29:07.050
You care to comment on that?

568
00:29:08.670 --> 00:29:11.950
I wouldn't know how.
I'm... I'm stunned.

569
00:29:11.950 --> 00:29:15.430
Well. that... That watch.
That's a rarity.

570
00:29:15.430 --> 00:29:17.570
I haven't seen
one of those in years

571
00:29:17.570 --> 00:29:19.430
and especially
not that vintage.

572
00:29:19.430 --> 00:29:21.190
Would you mind if
I took a closer look?

573
00:29:21.190 --> 00:29:22.950
He's crazy about watches.

574
00:29:22.950 --> 00:29:24.670
- Sure.
- Ooh.

575
00:29:24.670 --> 00:29:27.570
That looks like someone's been
playing with toxic chemicals.

576
00:29:27.570 --> 00:29:30.400
Caught you
red-handed so to speak.

577
00:29:30.400 --> 00:29:33.470
- What?
- Isopropyl alcohol maybe?

578
00:29:33.470 --> 00:29:35.980
In pure form it
can cause skin rashes

579
00:29:35.990 --> 00:29:39.640
if you were to use it to
clean your skin of what?

580
00:29:39.640 --> 00:29:41.400
Blood. maybe?

581
00:29:41.400 --> 00:29:43.640
Detectives. I am a banker.

582
00:29:43.640 --> 00:29:46.190
I use sanitizer
after every hand I shake

583
00:29:46.190 --> 00:29:48.160
and I shake a lot of hands.

584
00:29:48.160 --> 00:29:50.430
Now. if you wouldn't mind.
I'd appreciate if you directed

585
00:29:50.430 --> 00:29:52.260
any other questions
to my lawyer.

586
00:29:52.260 --> 00:29:54.290
- Mm-hmm.
- Deal.

587
00:29:54.300 --> 00:29:56.600
Uh. but in terms of getting
to work on time.

588
00:29:56.610 --> 00:29:59.670
I wouldn't worry.
See. we took your advice.

589
00:29:59.670 --> 00:30:01.640
That's a copy of
the search warrant

590
00:30:01.640 --> 00:30:03.260
that's gone to your branch.

591
00:30:03.260 --> 00:30:05.570
so we might beat you there.
but either way. see you soon.

592
00:30:20.810 --> 00:30:22.880
Irregularities
all over the place.

593
00:30:22.880 --> 00:30:26.980
Here's a student claiming
$400.000 in overseas income.

594
00:30:26.990 --> 00:30:32.050
Oh. this client owns three
homes on $2.400.000 borrowed.

595
00:30:32.050 --> 00:30:35.120
hairdresser.

596
00:30:35.120 --> 00:30:38.190
Ooh. Coffee ring and all.

597
00:30:38.190 --> 00:30:40.640
Oh. my God.
If you tried this at my bank.

598
00:30:40.640 --> 00:30:42.230
they would taser you
in the face.

599
00:30:42.230 --> 00:30:45.230
And then they'd file
a suspicious transaction report.

600
00:30:54.640 --> 00:30:58.330
Adrian Henning. we're placing
you under arrest.

601
00:30:58.330 --> 00:31:00.230
On what charge?

602
00:31:00.230 --> 00:31:04.920
Today? Conspiracy to commit
fraud and money laundering.

603
00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:07.190
But we'll see
what tomorrow brings.

604
00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:15.810
Mr. Grayson's network
funnelled dozens

605
00:31:15.810 --> 00:31:18.470
of fraudulent clients towards
Mr. Henning's bank.

606
00:31:18.470 --> 00:31:20.430
where they were
rubber stamped for loans.

607
00:31:20.430 --> 00:31:22.360
Allegedly.

608
00:31:22.360 --> 00:31:25.360
The initial audits suggest
it's been happening over a year.

609
00:31:25.360 --> 00:31:27.950
Now. are you telling me
your client--

610
00:31:27.950 --> 00:31:29.980
Theo. I thought
we were having lunch.

611
00:31:29.990 --> 00:31:32.740
You wanna talk hypotheticals?
I'm all ears.

612
00:31:32.740 --> 00:31:35.920
Otherwise--
- Alright. okay. Okay.

613
00:31:37.710 --> 00:31:41.950
Hypothetically speaking.
your client killed Jesse Grayson

614
00:31:41.950 --> 00:31:43.850
to hide his own
criminal activity

615
00:31:43.850 --> 00:31:45.640
at Hemisphere Savings & Loans.

616
00:31:45.640 --> 00:31:47.670
Mr. Henning has denied
any part in that fraud.

617
00:31:47.670 --> 00:31:49.330
And if you come at us claiming

618
00:31:49.330 --> 00:31:51.330
he planned to murder
Jesse Grayson--

619
00:31:51.330 --> 00:31:54.570
The traffic cams put him
at the condo on the night.

620
00:31:54.570 --> 00:31:58.670
Prints and DNA are all
over the murder weapon.

621
00:31:58.670 --> 00:32:00.400
You see cold-blooded intent.

622
00:32:00.400 --> 00:32:02.470
Perhaps I see something else.

623
00:32:03.640 --> 00:32:05.330
What would that be?

624
00:32:05.330 --> 00:32:08.260
Well. if I were to say.
and let's be clear I'm not.

625
00:32:08.260 --> 00:32:11.260
that my client knew
of a dangerous man

626
00:32:11.260 --> 00:32:12.810
who was defrauding his bank

627
00:32:12.810 --> 00:32:16.470
and asked this
dangerous man to stop.

628
00:32:16.470 --> 00:32:19.400
Oh. uh. if that's
your defence.

629
00:32:19.400 --> 00:32:22.090
that man would have
to be pretty dangerous

630
00:32:22.090 --> 00:32:24.260
for a murder charge to go away.

631
00:32:24.260 --> 00:32:26.330
I forget. who was it that

632
00:32:26.330 --> 00:32:29.050
brutally killed Timothy Fox
with an illegal weapon?

633
00:32:29.050 --> 00:32:31.810
Oh. right. Jesse Grayson.

634
00:32:31.810 --> 00:32:34.430
When your delusions
subside. call me.

635
00:32:34.430 --> 00:32:36.710
We'll start talking
in absolutes.

636
00:32:37.540 --> 00:32:39.430
Thanks for the shawarma.

637
00:32:51.540 --> 00:32:54.190
- Self-defence?
- It's looking that way.

638
00:32:54.190 --> 00:32:55.640
Prints left everywhere.

639
00:32:55.640 --> 00:32:57.540
murder weapon came
from Grayson's armoury.

640
00:32:57.540 --> 00:32:59.920
Okay. But you know that just
because it's not premeditated

641
00:32:59.920 --> 00:33:01.950
does not mean
it's not intentional.

642
00:33:01.950 --> 00:33:03.810
Yeah. all they have to do
is convince the jury

643
00:33:03.810 --> 00:33:05.360
that Henning
feared for his life.

644
00:33:05.360 --> 00:33:07.260
Caldwell does that. he'll walk.
- No. no. no.

645
00:33:07.260 --> 00:33:09.850
Grayson was attacked
from behind by surprise.

646
00:33:09.850 --> 00:33:13.780
He ad a whole arsenal of
weapons. but. uh. none in hand.

647
00:33:13.780 --> 00:33:16.430
He wasn't the aggressor.
- Yeah. not this time.

648
00:33:16.430 --> 00:33:18.570
Exactly. That's the issue.

649
00:33:18.570 --> 00:33:21.020
Grayson's a killer. Henning
at best is a family man.

650
00:33:21.020 --> 00:33:23.780
at worst. Robin Hood
giving houses to the poor.

651
00:33:23.780 --> 00:33:26.640
We need to dismantle
the folk hero narrative

652
00:33:26.640 --> 00:33:28.600
and put the blood
back on his hands.

653
00:33:28.610 --> 00:33:30.880
- Not this time.
- What?

654
00:33:30.880 --> 00:33:32.540
What she said.

655
00:33:32.540 --> 00:33:35.400
Grayson wasn't
the aggressor this time.

656
00:33:35.400 --> 00:33:39.360
This whole thing started when
one fraud collided with another.

657
00:33:39.360 --> 00:33:41.090
If Henning in any way.

658
00:33:41.090 --> 00:33:43.710
in any way. conspired
to kill the imposter...

659
00:33:43.710 --> 00:33:45.990
His self-defence
goes out the window.

660
00:33:47.190 --> 00:33:50.500
Yeah. you connect Henning
to the murder of Timothy Fox.

661
00:33:50.500 --> 00:33:52.810
I can put him away.
- Hmm.

662
00:33:52.810 --> 00:33:54.980
Back to fraud number one.

663
00:33:54.990 --> 00:33:56.950
Joy of joys.

664
00:34:01.300 --> 00:34:02.920
Hey.

665
00:34:04.500 --> 00:34:07.160
How's. uh. how's Josh?

666
00:34:07.160 --> 00:34:09.160
He's scared.

667
00:34:09.160 --> 00:34:12.810
Adrian. these things that
they're saying that you've done.

668
00:34:12.810 --> 00:34:14.430
Make it make sense.

669
00:34:14.430 --> 00:34:16.640
- I was protecting us.
- Don't you dare.

670
00:34:16.640 --> 00:34:19.570
Remember the other night.
we were coming home from dinner

671
00:34:19.570 --> 00:34:21.500
and there was that guy out
front of our house.

672
00:34:21.500 --> 00:34:24.230
You remember that?
He was threatening us. Tamara.

673
00:34:24.230 --> 00:34:26.160
He threatened to
hurt you and Josh.

674
00:34:26.160 --> 00:34:28.500
- What?
- I need...

675
00:34:28.500 --> 00:34:30.740
I need you to
tell him what you saw.

676
00:34:30.740 --> 00:34:32.090
Okay?

677
00:34:34.610 --> 00:34:36.500
The bank's lawyers advised us
not to talk to you guys.

678
00:34:36.500 --> 00:34:38.160
Oh. don't worry.
You can tell the bank's lawyers

679
00:34:38.160 --> 00:34:40.230
that we're not here to talk
about mortgage fraud.

680
00:34:40.230 --> 00:34:41.950
We're here to talk
about two dead bodies.

681
00:34:41.950 --> 00:34:44.120
What was
Adrian Henning's involvement

682
00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:46.020
with 227 Alton Drive?

683
00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:48.810
Mr. Henning kept a close tab
on that file.

684
00:34:48.810 --> 00:34:51.020
When the purchase
agreement came in.

685
00:34:51.020 --> 00:34:52.570
something agitated him.

686
00:34:52.570 --> 00:34:54.710
Something like a guy who
couldn't spell his last name?

687
00:34:54.710 --> 00:34:57.540
Is it normal for him to read
purchase agreements?

688
00:34:57.540 --> 00:35:00.020
No. He's a manager. He doesn't
handle customer transactions.

689
00:35:00.020 --> 00:35:02.230
Yet. here he is going
over this particular file

690
00:35:02.230 --> 00:35:03.670
with a magnifying glass.

691
00:35:03.670 --> 00:35:06.190
This one mattered to him. Why?

692
00:35:06.190 --> 00:35:09.570
I don't know what to tell you.
You make it all sound so dirty.

693
00:35:09.570 --> 00:35:12.360
- It does sound dirty.
- We help people buy homes.

694
00:35:12.360 --> 00:35:14.230
People like
Melissa Auerbach.

695
00:35:14.230 --> 00:35:16.290
A bartender just trying
to build a life.

696
00:35:16.300 --> 00:35:18.050
Um. hey. Graff?

697
00:35:22.740 --> 00:35:25.050
Henning discovered
the seller was sketchy.

698
00:35:25.050 --> 00:35:27.400
He looked into him.
found out he was an imposter.

699
00:35:27.400 --> 00:35:30.190
Yeah. he alerted Grayson.
told him to take care of it.

700
00:35:30.190 --> 00:35:32.920
Conspiracy to commit.
- If we can prove it.

701
00:35:34.300 --> 00:35:36.500
Dina. excuse me. but. um...

702
00:35:36.500 --> 00:35:38.780
Henning told us
that he was transferred

703
00:35:38.780 --> 00:35:40.400
to this branch
a couple years ago.

704
00:35:40.400 --> 00:35:41.670
Do you know where from?

705
00:35:41.670 --> 00:35:44.090
Um. Wellington Street branch.
Downtown.

706
00:35:44.090 --> 00:35:46.360
That's right across from
the Harbour View Lounge.

707
00:35:46.360 --> 00:35:48.360
We know someone
who works there.

708
00:35:51.020 --> 00:35:53.810
We get all types of money
guys at the bar.

709
00:35:53.810 --> 00:35:56.710
But Adrian seemed different.

710
00:35:56.710 --> 00:36:00.120
Open and-and... curious.
- And married.

711
00:36:00.120 --> 00:36:01.710
And he never tried
to hide that.

712
00:36:01.710 --> 00:36:04.050
We talked about it.
The ups and downs.

713
00:36:04.710 --> 00:36:06.500
We talked about everything.

714
00:36:06.500 --> 00:36:09.570
Melissa. Adrian Henning
has been accused

715
00:36:09.570 --> 00:36:11.290
of some very serious crimes.

716
00:36:11.300 --> 00:36:14.160
I'm still struggling
to believe that.

717
00:36:14.160 --> 00:36:16.600
You don't think he's
capable of such things?

718
00:36:16.610 --> 00:36:19.470
Maybe I didn't know him
as well as I thought I did.

719
00:36:22.090 --> 00:36:24.360
I know how this sounds.

720
00:36:24.360 --> 00:36:27.160
But I'm not some deluded ex.
I'm not pining.

721
00:36:28.740 --> 00:36:30.920
But our thing

722
00:36:30.920 --> 00:36:32.920
while it lasted.

723
00:36:32.920 --> 00:36:35.120
I don't know.

724
00:36:35.120 --> 00:36:38.300
Adrian inspired me to imagine
a different life for myself.

725
00:36:39.020 --> 00:36:40.430
A bigger one.

726
00:36:41.430 --> 00:36:43.670
And I didn't need it
to be real. but then--

727
00:36:43.670 --> 00:36:45.430
But then it became real.

728
00:36:45.430 --> 00:36:47.570
Yeah. you got pregnant.
he got cold feet.

729
00:36:47.570 --> 00:36:49.120
Yeah.

730
00:36:49.120 --> 00:36:52.230
And you weren't about to be
cast aside for nothing.

731
00:36:52.230 --> 00:36:54.120
I wasn't looking
to punish him.

732
00:36:54.120 --> 00:36:56.430
I just wanted
what he promised me.

733
00:36:56.430 --> 00:36:58.020
What he said was in reach.

734
00:36:58.020 --> 00:36:59.470
What was that?

735
00:37:00.740 --> 00:37:02.090
A home.

736
00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:09.540
Counselor.

737
00:37:09.540 --> 00:37:13.020
We've come across some new
information and. uh.

738
00:37:13.020 --> 00:37:15.290
wanted to give Mr. Henning
a chance to respond.

739
00:37:15.300 --> 00:37:17.230
Why is Mrs. Henning here?

740
00:37:17.230 --> 00:37:19.810
Mrs. Henning has some new
information as well.

741
00:37:19.810 --> 00:37:22.540
We'd hope Forester would be here

742
00:37:22.540 --> 00:37:24.850
so we could put
this all to bed. but...

743
00:37:24.850 --> 00:37:26.810
Tamara.

744
00:37:26.810 --> 00:37:28.470
Uh...

745
00:37:28.470 --> 00:37:30.020
Six nights ago.

746
00:37:30.020 --> 00:37:32.670
Adrian. Josh. and I were
walking home from the restaurant

747
00:37:32.670 --> 00:37:36.810
and this Jesse Grayson fellow.
he threatened us.

748
00:37:36.810 --> 00:37:38.880
- Mm-hmm.
- He threatened our son Josh.

749
00:37:38.880 --> 00:37:41.430
And he threatened
to kill us all.

750
00:37:41.430 --> 00:37:44.020
so whatever my husband did.

751
00:37:44.020 --> 00:37:46.230
he did out of self-defence.

752
00:37:47.120 --> 00:37:49.260
Thank you. Mrs. Henning. um.

753
00:37:49.260 --> 00:37:53.540
Would you be prepared to say all
that again in a court of law.

754
00:37:53.540 --> 00:37:56.050
in front of a gallery
of strangers.

755
00:37:56.050 --> 00:37:58.810
a jury of your peers. the press?

756
00:37:58.810 --> 00:38:01.190
Uh. yes. because
it's the truth.

757
00:38:02.400 --> 00:38:05.540
Uh. Mrs. Henning.
would you mind excusing us?

758
00:38:05.540 --> 00:38:10.050
We have some delicate matters
to discuss with your husband.

759
00:38:11.950 --> 00:38:13.950
No. no. I'll stay.

760
00:38:16.360 --> 00:38:19.190
We don't have any secrets.
Not anymore.

761
00:38:21.360 --> 00:38:23.640
Okay. uh. no secrets.

762
00:38:24.880 --> 00:38:28.670
Mr. Henning. who is
Melissa Auerbach to you?

763
00:38:30.570 --> 00:38:32.430
Uh...

764
00:38:32.430 --> 00:38:34.980
You spoke with her?
- We did.

765
00:38:34.990 --> 00:38:38.360
And you should know that
if this case goes to trial.

766
00:38:38.360 --> 00:38:40.500
she will be called to testify.

767
00:38:40.500 --> 00:38:43.260
My client's relationship
with Miss Auerbach

768
00:38:43.260 --> 00:38:45.160
has no bearing.

769
00:38:45.160 --> 00:38:47.810
Sometimes the least of
our sins speak the loudest.

770
00:38:47.810 --> 00:38:49.360
Mr. Henning.

771
00:38:49.360 --> 00:38:50.740
Less poetry. Detective.

772
00:38:50.740 --> 00:38:54.230
When your affair
with Miss Auerbach ended.

773
00:38:54.230 --> 00:38:58.160
you felt responsible.
You wanted to help her out.

774
00:38:58.160 --> 00:39:01.020
But. uh. you could hardly
buy a house for some bartender

775
00:39:01.020 --> 00:39:02.670
you had knocked up.

776
00:39:04.300 --> 00:39:06.330
Sorry. I guess you
left that part out.

777
00:39:07.880 --> 00:39:11.260
When you helped Melissa
and your baby.

778
00:39:11.260 --> 00:39:13.710
you had to do it
at arm's length.

779
00:39:13.710 --> 00:39:16.570
So you put her in touch with the
man who could make that happen.

780
00:39:16.570 --> 00:39:21.120
Grayson doctored the papers
and. um. she got her mortgage.

781
00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:24.290
You could help her with the
money and it'd all look clean.

782
00:39:24.300 --> 00:39:26.020
But bad luck.

783
00:39:26.020 --> 00:39:28.980
Melissa tried to buy
the house on Alton Drive.

784
00:39:28.990 --> 00:39:31.230
where the seller
was an imposter.

785
00:39:31.230 --> 00:39:36.540
You caught the con just in time
and informed Grayson to. uh.

786
00:39:36.540 --> 00:39:39.120
take care of it.

787
00:39:39.120 --> 00:39:41.090
I just wanted the guy
to back off--

788
00:39:41.090 --> 00:39:42.570
- Adrian.
- No. no.

789
00:39:42.570 --> 00:39:44.290
Grayson took it too far.

790
00:39:44.300 --> 00:39:46.570
Things were spiralling.
cops everywhere.

791
00:39:46.570 --> 00:39:48.160
and your lies woven
into this whole mess.

792
00:39:48.160 --> 00:39:50.880
Maybe he didn't go to Grayson's
that night to kill him.

793
00:39:50.880 --> 00:39:52.330
I didn't.

794
00:39:52.330 --> 00:39:54.540
Maybe you just wanted
him to smarten up.

795
00:39:54.540 --> 00:39:56.290
shut down his operation.

796
00:39:56.300 --> 00:39:58.120
and all Grayson had to do
was lay low.

797
00:39:58.120 --> 00:39:59.850
but not this guy.

798
00:39:59.850 --> 00:40:01.670
No. he's a head case.
a loose cannon.

799
00:40:01.670 --> 00:40:04.020
And as long as he was alive.

800
00:40:04.020 --> 00:40:06.570
everything you held dear
was at risk.

801
00:40:06.570 --> 00:40:08.430
Exactly. Mr. Henning
feared for his life

802
00:40:08.430 --> 00:40:09.850
and he defended himself.

803
00:40:09.850 --> 00:40:12.330
- A decent man in a bad spot.
- That's right.

804
00:40:12.330 --> 00:40:14.330
Beautiful family. Good job.

805
00:40:14.330 --> 00:40:17.570
Even the mortgage stuff. that's
a victimless crime. right?

806
00:40:17.570 --> 00:40:19.470
We're talking about
real estate here.

807
00:40:19.470 --> 00:40:21.090
Everyone's on the take.

808
00:40:21.090 --> 00:40:23.230
You were just keeping
with the flow of traffic.

809
00:40:23.230 --> 00:40:25.330
That's all the jury's
gonna hear. right?

810
00:40:25.330 --> 00:40:26.980
Except. um.

811
00:40:26.990 --> 00:40:29.640
Well. it doesn't work
that way anymore.

812
00:40:29.640 --> 00:40:31.570
Melissa Auerbach changes it.

813
00:40:32.430 --> 00:40:34.600
Make your point. Detective.

814
00:40:34.610 --> 00:40:37.090
The real victims
are the point.

815
00:40:37.090 --> 00:40:39.160
Right there in your own home.

816
00:40:39.160 --> 00:40:42.230
Your wife. Tamara.
Your son. Josh.

817
00:40:42.230 --> 00:40:44.050
You leave them out of this.

818
00:40:44.050 --> 00:40:45.950
Well. they're right in
the middle of it. Mr. Henning.

819
00:40:45.950 --> 00:40:47.470
because you put them there.

820
00:40:47.470 --> 00:40:50.020
Think about every time
you came home late

821
00:40:50.020 --> 00:40:51.850
and you saw
the pain on their faces.

822
00:40:51.850 --> 00:40:54.290
Every lie. every bad excuse.

823
00:40:54.300 --> 00:40:56.640
- I made a mistake.
- A mistake?

824
00:40:56.640 --> 00:40:58.540
No. no. no. Mr. Henning.
you're a cheat.

825
00:40:58.540 --> 00:41:00.850
You cheat at work.
you cheat on your wife.

826
00:41:00.850 --> 00:41:03.850
you cheat your unborn
child out of a father

827
00:41:03.850 --> 00:41:06.500
by bribing your
mistress with a house!

828
00:41:06.500 --> 00:41:08.020
Not a home.

829
00:41:08.020 --> 00:41:09.670
Hush money!

830
00:41:09.670 --> 00:41:12.090
Grayson was a threat
to my family.

831
00:41:12.090 --> 00:41:13.500
- A threat?
- Yes!

832
00:41:13.500 --> 00:41:15.230
Well. why didn't you go
to the police. huh?

833
00:41:15.230 --> 00:41:18.290
Sure. you'd broken the law.
but isn't a slap on the wrist

834
00:41:18.300 --> 00:41:20.360
better than committing murder?

835
00:41:20.360 --> 00:41:22.290
I told you Grayson
went too far!

836
00:41:22.300 --> 00:41:23.670
No. you went too far.

837
00:41:23.670 --> 00:41:25.500
It wasn't the fake documents
you were hiding.

838
00:41:25.500 --> 00:41:27.050
it was Melissa Auerbach's name.

839
00:41:27.050 --> 00:41:30.050
That was the reason
that you wanted all of this

840
00:41:30.050 --> 00:41:31.990
to stay hidden forever!

841
00:41:32.850 --> 00:41:34.290
You knew.

842
00:41:34.300 --> 00:41:37.570
The jury wasn't gonna see
some benevolent Robin Hood

843
00:41:37.570 --> 00:41:39.400
giving houses to the poor.

844
00:41:39.400 --> 00:41:42.920
They would see a lying banker.
a cheating husband.

845
00:41:42.920 --> 00:41:46.640
They would see you bashing
a fallen man's skull in

846
00:41:46.640 --> 00:41:48.570
until you could see his brains.

847
00:41:48.570 --> 00:41:50.230
That's enough. Detective.

848
00:41:50.230 --> 00:41:52.570
No. that's overkill.
Counselor. That is intent.

849
00:41:52.570 --> 00:41:55.230
The man was down.
He was not a threat anymore.

850
00:41:55.230 --> 00:41:58.090
And if you take this to trial.
this all comes out.

851
00:41:58.090 --> 00:42:00.230
And your family
will have to live

852
00:42:00.230 --> 00:42:01.640
through that horror in public.

853
00:42:01.640 --> 00:42:05.230
And for what?
A moment of bliss?

854
00:42:05.230 --> 00:42:07.570
To have your ego stroked
by a beautiful young woman?

855
00:42:07.570 --> 00:42:09.360
Detective Graff!

856
00:42:09.360 --> 00:42:12.260
So how much more pain do you
want them to go through. huh?

857
00:42:12.260 --> 00:42:14.050
I'm so sorry.

858
00:42:14.050 --> 00:42:17.260
I'm no Theo Forester.
but. uh. let's pretend.

859
00:42:17.260 --> 00:42:20.710
Excuse me. um. Mrs. Henning. um.

860
00:42:20.710 --> 00:42:23.430
But. um. how did you. uh.

861
00:42:23.430 --> 00:42:25.600
find out your husband
was having an affair?

862
00:42:25.610 --> 00:42:28.500
Did he accidentally whisper
it to you one night?

863
00:42:28.500 --> 00:42:31.260
Did he tell you
she was pregnant?

864
00:42:31.260 --> 00:42:35.020
And will your relationship be
with your husband's love child?

865
00:42:35.020 --> 00:42:36.470
Welcoming?

866
00:42:38.500 --> 00:42:40.570
Take your hands off me.

867
00:42:43.050 --> 00:42:46.260
Please. Somebody let me out.

868
00:42:54.740 --> 00:42:56.920
Just spoke with Forester.

869
00:42:56.920 --> 00:43:00.360
He got a guilty plea from
Adrian Henning. Second degree.

870
00:43:00.360 --> 00:43:01.950
No trial needed.

871
00:43:01.950 --> 00:43:04.290
I guess Henning found his heart.

872
00:43:04.300 --> 00:43:06.540
Or he just looked
at the numbers.

873
00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:11.190
You going home. Graff?

874
00:43:13.470 --> 00:43:14.880
I am.

875
00:43:21.990 --> 00:43:23.470
Night.

876
00:43:32.300 --> 00:43:34.360
difuze
